# Map every author identity used in this repository's history onto one person.
#
# Commits were made from three different git identities over time: a personal
# address, a university address, and GitHub's noreply address. They are all the
# same author, so collapse them into a single canonical entry.
#
# Format: <Canonical Name> <canonical@email> <commit@email>
# Docs:   https://git-scm.com/docs/gitmailmap
#
# Affects git shortlog, log, blame and other local git tooling. It has no effect
# on GitHub's contributor graph, which is computed server-side.

Efe Özan <efe052006@gmail.com> <efeozan@marun.edu.tr>
